var P1={ "rotate-trace": "Rotate the {n}x{n} matrix 90 degrees clockwise, in place conceptually (here we produce the result). The drill matrix is {m}. The index mapping to internalize is rot[i][j] = m[n-1-j][i]: the new row i is the old column i read bottom-to-top. Work it cell by cell before checking." };
var P2={ "rotate-trace": "Two ways to see it: layer by layer (each ring rotates as a cycle of four) or transpose-then-reverse-each-row (transpose swaps [i][j] with [j][i]; reversing rows completes the clockwise turn). Both are O(n^2) time and the layered version is O(1) extra space. Pick one and trace every assignment." };
